9adda26162dc40dd86f60c5b08dfe974b9e"},"seconds":28.871620655059814,"seed":495745103845987862,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we first need to determine which fraction in the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$ is the greatest and which is the least. To do this effectively, we'll convert each fraction to a decimal form for easier comparison.\n\n1. Convert $\\frac{3}{7}$ to a decimal:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286\n   \\]\n\n2. Convert $\\frac{4}{3}$ to a decimal:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333\n   \\]\n\n3. Convert $\\frac{11}{8}$ to a decimal:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\n   \\]\n\n4. Convert $\\frac{6}{16}$ to a decimal:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\n   \\]\n\nNow, we list the decimal equivalents of the fractions:\n- $\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286$\n- $\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333$\n- $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$\n- $\\frac{6}{16} = 0.375$\n\nNext, we identify the greatest and the least fractions:\n- The greatest fraction is $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$\n- The least fraction is $\\frac{6}{16} = 0.375$\n\nTo find the positive difference between the greatest and the least fractions, we subtract the least from the greatest:\n\\[\n1.375 - 0.375 = 1.000\n\\]\n\nExpressing this difference in simplest fractional form:\n\\[\n1.000 = \\frac{1}{1}\n\\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
